      "writtenOn": "2022-01-17T12:02:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Remi. Thank you for bringing this up. This change can\u0027t be merged into sc-mainline-prod because it depends on some Soong changes, which are not in sc-mainline-prod.\n\nThis CL only changed a few lines, so the chance of getting merge conflicts is small. Besides, the dexpreopt artifacts are stored on the system partition, rather than in the APEX. Therefore, this CL does not cause a diff in the module itself other than an entry in etc/systemserverclasspath.pb, which will not be used on S devices anyway, so merging this change into sc-mainline-prod does not make a difference.\n\nUnfortunately, we cannot revert this change because we want to enforce standalone system server jars to be dexopted, as system server jars are performance sensitive, and we already have checks for that:\n1. There is dexpreopt_check in the build system to check that dexpreopt artifacts are generated.\n2. There is an ongoing effort (aosp/1925695) to add a runtime check to reject APEX standalone system server jars that are not dexopted.",
      "parentUuid": "f68fb684_d5d4bbe2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "86c139aedb043ca5a50cd37baeca7309389b51fa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43653f60_bf095093",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-18T03:21:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the Soong changes be cherry-picked to sc-mainline-prod then, at least so that they don\u0027t require modules to take the merge conflicts ?\n\nIt\u0027s good that this particular change isn\u0027t a big conflict and likely won\u0027t affect R/S; but as a general rule we don\u0027t take changes that don\u0027t go to sc-mainline-prod in our modules because they increase risk of the first T-based release, where changes that were merged several months before would get pushed to public devices. This year such changes caused at least 2 large issues in resolv and cellbroadcast, so as a policy we try to avoid them. Looking at them on a case-by-case basis is risky, and merge conflicts can also pile up.\n\nIf the feature isn\u0027t developed in sc-mainline-prod (which would be better if it\u0027s affecting modules), could the checks be only enabled after t-mainline-prod is branched, when modules can start using it ?",
      "parentUuid": "8a3dc5d6_6202e412",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "86c139aedb043ca5a50cd37baeca7309389b51fa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
